From 8a414d6319c7892e01fb8861ea87fbacc4bf2e9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:03:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add AWS Lambda deploy support: DynamoDB-backed leads, SST
 config
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Add sst.config.ts (SST v3/Ion): sst.aws.Nextjs wrapping OpenNext for
  AWS Lambda + CloudFront hosting, plus a new sst.aws.Dynamo leads
  table (MoLeadsTable) linked to the site for least-privilege IAM.
- Add lib/dynamoLeads.ts: DynamoDB-backed lead storage (FlatLead shape
  matching the existing Prisma Lead columns 1:1) so the admin
  dashboard UI needs no changes.
- Wire lib/leadStore.ts and app/api/admin/leads/* to use DynamoDB
  first (when LEADS_TABLE is set), falling back to Prisma/Postgres
  (Vercel) and then the local-file dev fallback, in that order.
- Fix tsconfig.json: exclude .sst, sst.config.ts and sst-env.d.ts so
  next build's type-checker doesn't follow SST's generated Pulumi
  types via the triple-slash reference (fixes an unrelated SST
  internal type error in alb.ts that otherwise fails the build).
- Add @aws-sdk/client-dynamodb, @aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb, and sst as
  dependencies; ignore SST's generated .sst/ and sst-env.d.ts.

The local-file lead fallback (LEAD_STORE=file) cannot work on Lambda
because the deployed package directory is read-only (EROFS) — this
was caught by a test deploy to a "test" stage (CloudFront URL, not
the production domain) and verified fixed by submitting the live
contact form and confirming the record landed correctly in DynamoDB.

Vercel/Prisma remains the production backend for
mobehaviortherapy.com; this is purely additive, for an in-progress
migration to AWS (see project docs for HIPAA/BAA context). No DNS or
production traffic changes.

